-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THIS LICENCE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: anyone who modifies these files must publish
those modifications, but they may combine this code with differently licensed
code without relicensing their whole application.

This matters for one concrete reason. The GPL forbids imposing further
restrictions on users, and Apple's App Store terms impose exactly such
restrictions. The two are widely held to be incompatible - VLC was removed
from the App Store in 2011 over this. Choosing GPL here would make an iOS
release legally untenable. MPL-2.0 keeps the code open while leaving every
distribution channel available: Play Store, App Store, and a sideloaded APK
handed to someone directly.

